**Step 1:** List A = odd numbers from 1 to 10 = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}

**Step 2:** List B = multiples of 3 from 1 to 10 = {3, 6, 9}

**Step 3:** A ∪ B combines all elements, listing shared ones (3, 9) only once.

**A ∪ B = {1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9}**

**Verification:** n(A)=5, n(B)=3, n(A∩B)=2 (elements 3,9). n(A∪B) = 5+3−2 = 6, and the listed set has 6 elements
